FINAL_CIRCUIT = circuit","filename":"bell_state.py","framework":"Cirq","language":"python","status":"native"}],"description":"A two-qubit entanglement example with a return contract and distribution check.","descriptionJa":"出力形式と分布を確認できる、2量子ビットのエンタングルメント例です。","explanation":"H creates a superposition on q0, and CNOT copies the correlation into q1. Measuring the pair gives 00 or 11 with equal probability in the ideal circuit.","explanationJa":"Hでq0を重ね合わせ、CNOTでq1に相関を作ります。理想回路では測定結果は00または11に等確率で現れます。","explanationMd":"The Bell state $\frac{1}{\sqrt2}(|00\rangle+|11\rangle)$ is prepared by $H$ on qubit 0 followed by $\mathrm{CX}_{0\to1}$: starting from $|00\rangle$, $H\otimes I$ gives $\frac{1}{\sqrt2}(|00\rangle+|10\rangle)$, and CX then copies the control's value onto the target, $\frac{1}{\sqrt2}(|00\rangle+|11\rangle)$ — exactly the statevector this record's exact-state check compares against. Measuring both qubits in the computational basis yields $00$ or $11$ each with probability $1/2$ and never $01$ or $10$: the two outcomes are perfectly correlated even though neither qubit's individual outcome is determined before measurement, the operational signature of entanglement (this state violates a Bell/CHSH inequality; it cannot be reproduced by any local hidden-variable model tossing independent coins). Because it is the smallest circuit exhibiting genuine quantum correlation, the Bell state anchors teleportation, superdense coding, and entanglement-verification protocols throughout this catalog.","explanationMdJa":"ベル状態 $\frac{1}{\sqrt2}(|00\rangle+|11\rangle)$ は、量子ビット0への$H$の後に $\mathrm{CX}_{0\to1}$ を適用して作ります。$|00\rangle$から出発すると $H\otimes I$ で $\frac{1}{\sqrt2}(|00\rangle+|10\rangle)$ になり、CXが制御の値を対象にコピーして $\frac{1}{\sqrt2}(|00\rangle+|11\rangle)$ となります。これがこの項目の厳密な状態チェックが比較する状態ベクトルです。両量子ビットを計算基底で測定すると00または11がそれぞれ確率$1/2$で得られ、01や10は現れません。測定前にどちらの結果も個別には決まっていないにもかかわらず2つの結果は完全に相関しており、これがエンタングルメントの操作的な特徴です(この状態はベル/CHSH不等式を破り、独立なコイン投げによる局所隠れ変数モデルでは再現できません)。真の量子相関を示す最小の回路であるため、ベル状態はこのカタログ全体でテレポーテーションや超密符号化、エンタングルメント検証プロトコルの基礎になっています。","exportStatus":"OpenQASM 3 available · lossless gate mapping","framework":"Qiskit","introduction":"The Bell state is compact enough for a first experiment and rich enough to show that measurement outcomes can be correlated without choosing a classical bit in advance.","introductionJa":"ベル状態は最初の実験に十分コンパクトでありながら、測定前に古典ビットを選ばずに相関が現れることを示せます。","literature":[{"authors":"John S. Bell","relevance":"Introduces the Bell inequality that distinguishes entangled correlations, such as the Bell state, from any local hidden-variable model.","relevanceJa":"ベル状態のようなエンタングルした相関を局所隠れ変数モデルと区別するベル不等式の原論文です。","title":"On the Einstein Podolsky Rosen Paradox","url":"https://doi.org/10.1103/physicsphysiquefizika.1.195","year":"1964"},{"authors":"Michael A. Nielsen and Isaac L. Chuang","relevance":"Standard graduate textbook covering the single- and two-qubit gate definitions, matrix identities, and circuit primitives this record states.","relevanceJa":"この項目が示す1・2量子ビットゲートの定義、行列恒等式、回路プリミティブを扱う標準的な大学院教科書です。","title":"Quantum Computation and Quantum Information: 10th Anniversary Edition","url":"https://doi.org/10.1017/cbo9780511976667","year":"2010"}],"metadata":[{"label":"State","value":"(|00⟩ + |11⟩)/√2"},{"label":"Ideal P(00)","value":"0.5"},{"label":"Ideal P(11)","value":"0.5"}],"provenance":"Textbook reference","relatedSlugs":["hadamard-gate","ghz-state-pennylane"],"resources":[{"label":"Qubits","value":"2"},{"label":"Depth","value":"2 gates"},{"label":"Outcomes","value":"00 / 11"}],"slug":"bell-state-qiskit","source":{"contributor":"LeonaQ public reference set","kind":"curated_reference","license":"CC BY 4.0-compatible reference metadata","reviewedBy":"LeonaQ curation pass","title":"Quantum Computation and Quantum Information: 10th Anniversary Edition","url":"https://doi.org/10.1017/cbo9780511976667"},"sourceCoverage":{"hardware":"unknown","simulation":"unknown","theory":"unknown"},"status":"verified","tags":["entanglement","intro","verification"],"title":"Bell state measurement","titleJa":"ベル状態の測定","topics":["state","state-preparation"],"updatedAt":"2026-08-12","verification":"Exact state check · return contract passed","verificationDetails":{"method":"Statevector and sampled distribution compared with the ideal Bell-state support.","result":"Pass · only 00 and 11 appear in the ideal measurement distribution."},"verificationMethods":["exact_simulation","statistical_counts","invariant_checks","research_paper"],"visualization":{"operations":[{"label":"H","qubits":[0],"tone":"accent"},{"label":"CX","qubits":[0,1],"tone":"ok"}],"outcomes":[{"label":"00","probability":0.5},{"label":"11","probability":0.5}],"wires":["q[0]","q[1]"]}}

{"algorithmFamily":"Controlled gate","category":"gates","categoryLabel":"Gates","categoryLabelJa":"ゲート","codeVariants":[{"code":"OPENQASM 3.0;
include "stdgates.inc";
qubit[2] q;
cx q[0], q[1];","filename":"controlled-x.qasm","framework":"OpenQASM 3.0","language":"openqasm","status":"native"}],"description":"The canonical two-qubit controlled operation used to create correlation and entanglement.","descriptionJa":"相関とエンタングルメントを作る、代表的な2量子ビット制御演算です。","explanation":"CX leaves the target unchanged for control 0 and applies X for control 1. With H on the control, it creates the Bell-state pattern.","explanationJa":"CXは制御0なら対象を変えず、制御1ならXを適用します。制御側にHを置くとベル状態の構造になります。","explanationMd":"Controlled-$X$ (CNOT) acts on two qubits as $\mathrm{CX}|c,t\rangle = |c, t\oplus c\rangle$: the target flips exactly when the control is $|1\rangle$, the truth table this record checks directly against the four computational-basis inputs. In matrix form, $\mathrm{CX}=|0\rangle\langle0|\otimes I + |1\rangle\langle1|\otimes X$, a $4\times4$ permutation matrix that is its own inverse, $\mathrm{CX}^2=I$. Applied after a Hadamard on the control, $\mathrm{CX}(H\otimes I)|00\rangle = \frac{1}{\sqrt2}(|00\rangle+|11\rangle)$, the Bell state this catalog's entangling-action check reproduces — the second half of the verification claim. CNOT is a maximally entangling two-qubit gate: together with arbitrary single-qubit rotations it forms a universal gate set, and physically it is the standard native (or compiled) two-qubit interaction most hardware backends expose, making it the workhorse for building larger controlled operations.","explanationMdJa":"制御$X$(CNOT)は2量子ビットに対し $\mathrm{CX}|c,t\rangle = |c, t\oplus c\rangle$ と作用します。つまり制御が$|1\rangle$のときだけ対象が反転し、これは4つの計算基底入力に対して直接確認できる真理値表です。行列表現では $\mathrm{CX}=|0\rangle\langle0|\otimes I + |1\rangle\langle1|\otimes X$ という$4\times4$の置換行列で、自分自身の逆 $\mathrm{CX}^2=I$ を満たします。制御側にHadamardをかけた後に適用すると $\mathrm{CX}(H\otimes I)|00\rangle = \frac{1}{\sqrt2}(|00\rangle+|11\rangle)$ となり、これがこのカタログのエンタングル作用チェックが再現するベル状態、つまり検証主張の後半です。CNOTは最大限にエンタングルする2量子ビットゲートで、任意の1量子ビット回転と組み合わせると万能ゲート集合になり、物理的にもほとんどのハードウェアが提供するネイティブ(または合成された)2量子ビット相互作用として、より大きな制御演算を組み立てる基礎になります。","exportStatus":"Native OpenQASM 3 · direct framework snippets available","framework":"OpenQASM 3.0","introduction":"Controlled-X is the bridge between a single-qubit operation and a multi-qubit circuit contract.","introductionJa":"制御Xは、単一量子ビット演算と多量子ビット回路の契約をつなぎます。","literature":[{"authors":"Michael A. Nielsen and Isaac L. Chuang","relevance":"Standard graduate textbook covering the single- and two-qubit gate definitions, matrix identities, and circuit primitives this record states.","relevanceJa":"この項目が示す1・2量子ビットゲートの定義、行列恒等式、回路プリミティブを扱う標準的な大学院教科書です。","title":"Quantum Computation and Quantum Information: 10th Anniversary Edition","url":"https://doi.org/10.1017/cbo9780511976667","year":"2010"}],"metadata":[{"label":"Control","value":"q[0]"},{"label":"Target","value":"q[1]"},{"label":"Universal role","value":"Entangling basis gate"}],"provenance":"Curated reference","relatedSlugs":["bell-state-qiskit","swap-gate"],"resources":[{"label":"Qubits","value":"2"},{"label":"Depth","value":"1 gate"},{"label":"Outcomes","value":"conditional"}],"slug":"controlled-x-gate","source":{"kind":"curated_reference","license":"CC BY 4.0-compatible reference metadata","reviewedBy":"Leona Quantum curation pass","title":"OpenQASM 3 standard gate set","url":"https://openqasm.com/language/gates.html"},"sourceCoverage":{"hardware":"unknown","simulation":"unknown","theory":"unknown"},"status":"verified","tags":["controlled gate","entanglement","two qubit"],"title":"Controlled-X gate","titleJa":"制御Xゲート","topics":["gate-primitive"],"updatedAt":"2026-07-15","verification":"Truth-table and entangling action check","verificationDetails":{"method":"Compare the computational-basis truth table and Bell-state construction.","result":"Pass · target flips exactly when the control is |1⟩."},"verificationMethods":["truth_table","construction","research_paper"],"visualization":{"operations":[{"label":"CX","qubits":[0,1],"tone":"ok"}],"outcomes":[{"label":"Control 0","probability":0.5},{"label":"Control 1","probability":0.5}],"wires":["q[0]","q[1]"]}}

{"algorithmFamily":"GHZ / entanglement","category":"states","categoryLabel":"States","categoryLabelJa":"状態","codeVariants":[{"code":"import pennylane as qml

dev = qml.device("default.qubit", wires=4)

@qml.qnode(dev)
def ghz_state():
    qml.Hadamard(wires=0)
    for wire in range(1, 4):
        qml.CNOT(wires=[0, wire])
    return qml.probs(wires=range(4))

FINAL_CIRCUIT = ghz_state","filename":"ghz_state.py","framework":"PennyLane","language":"python","status":"native"},{"code":"from qiskit import QuantumCircuit

qc = QuantumCircuit(4)
qc.h(0)
for wire in range(1, 4):
    qc.cx(0, wire)

FINAL_CIRCUIT = qc","filename":"ghz_state.py","framework":"Qiskit","language":"python","status":"native"}],"description":"A reusable GHZ state preparation circuit with simulator-only evidence.","descriptionJa":"シミュレータで検証した範囲を明示した、再利用可能なGHZ状態準備回路です。","explanation":"One Hadamard creates the branch, then CNOTs fan that branch from q0 to the remaining wires. In the ideal model, all measured bits agree.","explanationJa":"1つのHで分岐を作り、CNOTをq0から他のワイヤへ広げます。理想モデルでは測定ビットがすべて一致します。","explanationMd":"The GHZ state on $n=4$ wires, $\frac{1}{\sqrt2}(|0000\rangle+|1111\rangle)$, extends the Bell-state pattern: one Hadamard on wire 0 creates the branch, $\frac{1}{\sqrt2}(|0000\rangle+|1000\rangle)$, and CNOTs fan it from wire 0 to wires 1, 2, 3 in turn, each spreading the correlation until all four qubits agree. This record's check confirms the circuit structure and the ideal simulator support — probability mass only on $0000$ and $1111$ — which is what the entry's own caveat scopes: simulator evidence, not a hardware noise measurement. Unlike the Bell state, GHZ correlations are fragile: a single bit- or phase-flip error on any one of the four qubits during preparation collapses the perfect two-outcome distribution, which is exactly why GHZ fidelity is used as a standard multi-qubit benchmark for characterizing crosstalk and coherence on real devices — distinct from the ideal-circuit claim made here.","explanationMdJa":"4本のワイヤ上のGHZ状態 $\frac{1}{\sqrt2}(|0000\rangle+|1111\rangle)$ は、ベル状態のパターンを拡張したものです。ワイヤ0へのHadamardで分岐を作り $\frac{1}{\sqrt2}(|0000\rangle+|1000\rangle)$ となった後、CNOTをワイヤ0から1、2、3へ順に適用し、相関を次々と広げて最終的に4量子ビットすべてを一致させます。この項目のチェックが確認するのは回路構造と、確率が0000と1111にのみ乗る理想シミュレータでの分布であり、これはエントリ自身の注記が範囲とする「シミュレータのみの証拠」です。ベル状態と異なり、GHZ相関は壊れやすく、準備中に4量子ビットのいずれか1つでビット反転や位相反転誤りが起きるだけで完璧な2状態分布は崩れます。だからこそGHZ忠実度は実機のクロストークやコヒーレンスを特徴づける標準的な多量子ビットベンチマークとして使われますが、それはここで主張する理想回路の結果とは別の話です。","exportStatus":"Native PennyLane and Qiskit · OpenQASM conversion classified","framework":"PennyLane","introduction":"GHZ preparation extends the Bell-state pattern to a small register and makes the distinction between local operations and global correlation visible.","introductionJa":"GHZ準備はベル状態のパターンを小さなレジスタに拡張し、局所操作と全体相関の違いを示します。","literature":[{"authors":"Michael A. Nielsen and Isaac L. Chuang","relevance":"Standard graduate textbook covering the single- and two-qubit gate definitions, matrix identities, and circuit primitives this record states.","relevanceJa":"この項目が示す1・2量子ビットゲートの定義、行列恒等式、回路プリミティブを扱う標準的な大学院教科書です。","title":"Quantum Computation and Quantum Information: 10th Anniversary Edition","url":"https://doi.org/10.1017/cbo9780511976667","year":"2010"}],"metadata":[{"label":"State","value":"(|0000⟩ + |1111⟩)/√2"},{"label":"Ideal support","value":"2 of 16 outcomes"},{"label":"Evidence","value":"Simulator only"}],"provenance":"Framework example","relatedSlugs":["bell-state-qiskit","hadamard-gate"],"resources":[{"label":"Qubits","value":"4"},{"label":"Depth","value":"2 layers"},{"label":"Outcomes","value":"0000 / 1111"}],"slug":"ghz-state-pennylane","source":{"kind":"curated_reference","license":"CC BY 4.0-compatible reference metadata","reviewedBy":"LeonaQ curation pass","title":"PennyLane quantum operations reference","url":"https://docs.pennylane.ai/en/stable/introduction/circuits.html"},"sourceCoverage":{"hardware":"unknown","simulation":"unknown","theory":"unknown"},"status":"verified_caveats","tags":["state preparation","pennylane","simulator","entanglement"],"title":"GHZ state preparation","titleJa":"GHZ状態の準備","topics":["state","state-preparation"],"updatedAt":"2026-07-09","verification":"Structural checks passed · simulator-only caveat","verificationDetails":{"caveat":"This public reference does not claim hardware noise validation.","method":"Circuit structure and ideal simulator probabilities checked for four wires.","result":"Pass · support is 0000 and 1111 in the ideal simulator."},"verificationMethods":["exact_simulation","invariant_checks"],"visualization":{"operations":[{"label":"H","qubits":[0],"tone":"accent"},{"label":"CX","qubits":[0,1],"tone":"ok"},{"label":"CX","qubits":[0,2],"tone":"ok"},{"label":"CX","qubits":[0,3],"tone":"ok"}],"outcomes":[{"label":"0000","probability":0.5},{"label":"1111","probability":0.5}],"wires":["q[0]","q[1]","q[2]","q[3]"]}}

