FINAL_CIRCUIT = flip","filename":"pauli-x.py","framework":"PennyLane","language":"python","status":"native"}],"description":"A bit-flip operator that makes the relationship between a circuit and its truth table explicit.","descriptionJa":"回路と真理値表の関係を明確にするビット反転演算子です。","explanation":"X swaps the computational basis states. On a Bloch sphere it is a π rotation around the x axis; on a classical-looking input it behaves as a deterministic bit flip.","explanationJa":"Xは計算基底状態を入れ替えます。ブロッホ球ではx軸周りのπ回転で、古典的に見える入力では決定的なビット反転として動作します。","explanationMd":"Pauli-$X$ is the bit-flip operator $X = \begin{pmatrix}0&1\\1&0\end{pmatrix}$, the quantum analogue of a classical NOT gate. On computational basis states it acts exactly as a truth table: $X|0\rangle=|1\rangle$ and $X|1\rangle=|0\rangle$, which is the identity this record's basis-state simulation checks directly rather than inferring from a general formula. $X$ is Hermitian and unitary with $X^2=I$, so it is its own inverse, and its eigenstates are $|+\rangle=\frac{1}{\sqrt2}(|0\rangle+|1\rangle)$ and $|-\rangle=\frac{1}{\sqrt2}(|0\rangle-|1\rangle)$ with eigenvalues $+1$ and $-1$. Geometrically, $X$ is a $\pi$ rotation of the Bloch sphere about the $x$-axis. Because $X$, together with $Y$ and $Z$, generates the full single-qubit Pauli group ($XY=iZ$ and cyclic permutations), it anchors error models, stabilizer codes, and controlled two-qubit gates such as CNOT.","explanationMdJa":"パウリ$X$はビット反転演算子 $X=\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\1&0\end{pmatrix}$ で、古典NOTゲートの量子版です。計算基底では真理値表そのものの動作をし、$X|0\rangle=|1\rangle$、$X|1\rangle=|0\rangle$ となります。これは一般公式からの推測ではなく、基底状態シミュレーションで直接確認できる恒等式です。$X$はエルミートかつユニタリで $X^2=I$、つまり自分自身の逆演算です。固有状態は$|+\rangle=\frac{1}{\sqrt2}(|0\rangle+|1\rangle)$と$|-\rangle=\frac{1}{\sqrt2}(|0\rangle-|1\rangle)$で、固有値はそれぞれ$+1$、$-1$です。幾何学的にはブロッホ球の$x$軸周りの$\pi$回転にあたります。$Y$、$Z$とともに1量子ビットのパウリ群を生成し($XY=iZ$とその巡回)、ビット反転誤りモデルやスタビライザー符号、CNOTのような制御ゲートの基礎になります。","exportStatus":"Native OpenQASM 3 · direct framework snippets available","framework":"OpenQASM 3.0","introduction":"Pauli-X is the quantum analogue of a classical NOT gate and a useful anchor for operator-level explanations.","introductionJa":"パウリXは古典的なNOTゲートに対応し、演算子レベルの説明の基準になります。","literature":[{"authors":"Michael A. Nielsen and Isaac L. Chuang","relevance":"Standard graduate textbook covering the single- and two-qubit gate definitions, matrix identities, and circuit primitives this record states.","relevanceJa":"この項目が示す1・2量子ビットゲートの定義、行列恒等式、回路プリミティブを扱う標準的な大学院教科書です。","title":"Quantum Computation and Quantum Information: 10th Anniversary Edition","url":"https://doi.org/10.1017/cbo9780511976667","year":"2010"}],"metadata":[{"label":"Matrix","value":"[[0, 1], [1, 0]]"},{"label":"Rotation","value":"π around X"},{"label":"Input","value":"Computational basis"}],"provenance":"Curated reference","relatedSlugs":["hadamard-gate","bell-state-qiskit"],"resources":[{"label":"Qubits","value":"1"},{"label":"Depth","value":"1 gate"},{"label":"Outcomes","value":"1 per input"}],"slug":"pauli-x-operator","source":{"kind":"curated_reference","license":"CC BY 4.0-compatible reference metadata","reviewedBy":"LeonaQ curation pass","title":"OpenQASM 3 standard gate set","url":"https://openqasm.com/language/gates.html"},"sourceCoverage":{"hardware":"unknown","simulation":"unknown","theory":"unknown"},"status":"verified","tags":["pauli","bit flip","foundations"],"title":"Pauli-X operator","titleJa":"パウリX演算子","topics":["operator"],"updatedAt":"2026-07-14","verification":"Truth-table check · |0⟩ and |1⟩ exchanged","verificationDetails":{"method":"Exact basis-state simulation with computational-basis measurement.","result":"Pass · X|0⟩ = |1⟩ and X|1⟩ = |0⟩."},"verificationMethods":["truth_table","research_paper"],"visualization":{"operations":[{"label":"X","qubits":[0],"tone":"ok"}],"outcomes":[{"label":"1 from |0⟩","probability":1}],"wires":["q[0]"]}}

