z q;","filename":"pauli-z.qasm","framework":"OpenQASM 3.0","language":"openqasm","status":"native"}],"description":"A phase-flip gate whose behavior is invisible to a basis measurement until interference is introduced.","descriptionJa":"基底測定だけでは見えず、干渉で現れる位相反転ゲートです。","explanation":"Z|0⟩ = |0⟩ and Z|1⟩ = -|1⟩. Applied inside a superposition, the relative phase changes later interference.","explanationJa":"Z|0⟩ = |0⟩、Z|1⟩ = -|1⟩です。重ね合わせの中では相対位相が変わり、後の干渉に現れます。","explanationMd":"Pauli-$Z$ is the phase-flip operator $Z=\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\0&-1\end{pmatrix}$. On the computational basis, $Z|0\rangle=|0\rangle$ and $Z|1\rangle=-|1\rangle$, exactly the identity checked here by comparing the matrix action against both basis states directly. Because a measurement in the computational basis cannot distinguish $|1\rangle$ from $-|1\rangle$ (both give outcome "1" with probability 1), $Z$ is invisible on a bare basis state; its effect only shows up once the qubit is in a superposition, where the flipped sign changes how later amplitudes interfere — the point the entry's own explanation makes. $Z$ is Hermitian and unitary with $Z^2=I$, so it is its own inverse, and it is a $\pi$ rotation of the Bloch sphere about the $z$-axis. $Z$ underlies the phase-kickback trick used in Deutsch–Jozsa-style oracles and phase-flip error models in stabilizer codes.","explanationMdJa":"パウリ$Z$は位相反転演算子 $Z=\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\0&-1\end{pmatrix}$ です。計算基底では $Z|0\rangle=|0\rangle$、$Z|1\rangle=-|1\rangle$ となり、これは両方の基底状態に対する行列作用を直接比較して確認する恒等式です。計算基底での測定は$|1\rangle$と$-|1\rangle$を区別できない(どちらも確率1で「1」)ため、$Z$は単体の基底状態には見えず、重ね合わせの中で初めて符号の反転が後の干渉に現れます。これはこの項目の説明が指摘している点です。$Z$はエルミートかつユニタリで $Z^2=I$、自分自身の逆演算であり、ブロッホ球の$z$軸周りの$\pi$回転に相当します。$Z$はDeutsch–Jozsa型オラクルで使われる位相キックバックや、スタビライザー符号における位相反転誤りモデルの基礎になります。","exportStatus":"Native OpenQASM 3 · direct framework snippets available","framework":"OpenQASM 3.0","introduction":"Pauli-Z is the smallest useful record for explaining why phase is operational even when probabilities 