cp(pi/8) q[3], q[0];","filename":"qft_resource_screen.qasm","framework":"OpenQASM 3.0","language":"openqasm","status":"native"}],"description":"A resource-focused QFT construction with a readable compile comparison.","descriptionJa":"読みやすいコンパイル比較を備えた、リソース重視のQFT構成です。","explanation":"Hadamards create the Fourier basis and controlled phase rotations encode relative phase relationships. The final swap layer is optional depending on bit-order convention, so the catalog keeps that choice explicit.","explanationJa":"Hでフーリエ基底を作り、制御位相回転で相対位相を表現します。最後のswapはビット順の規約で任意になるため、カタログでは選択を明示します。","explanationMd":"The QFT maps computational basis states to a Fourier basis: $\mathrm{QFT}|j\rangle=\frac{1}{\sqrt{2^n}}\sum_{k=0}^{2^n-1}e^{2\pi i jk/2^n}|k\rangle$ for an $n$-qubit register. The standard circuit applies a Hadamard on the top qubit, then controlled phase rotations $R_k=\mathrm{diag}(1,e^{2\pi i/2^k})$ from every later qubit into it, repeats for each qubit in turn, and optionally reverses qubit order with a final SWAP layer depending on bit-order convention — the layer this record's metadata keeps explicit. The circuit uses $n$ Hadamards and $\binom{n}{2}$ controlled-phase gates, giving $O(n^2)$ total gates versus the classical FFT's $O(N\log N)=O(2^n\cdot n)$ arithmetic operations on a full amplitude vector — an exponential gate-count saving, but only over quantum amplitudes that must then be sampled, not a free classical output vector. This record's check is a parser/compile-compatibility comparison across the export path, not a numerical circuit-correctness proof.","explanationMdJa":"QFTは計算基底状態をフーリエ基底に写します: $n$量子ビットレジスタに対し $\mathrm{QFT}|j\rangle=\frac{1}{\sqrt{2^n}}\sum_{k=0}^{2^n-1}e^{2\pi i jk/2^n}|k\rangle$。標準的な回路は最上位量子ビットにHadamardをかけ、後続の各量子ビットから制御位相回転$R_k=\mathrm{diag}(1,e^{2\pi i/2^k})$をそこへ適用し、これを各量子ビットについて繰り返した後、ビット順の規約次第で最後にSWAP層で順序を反転します。この層はこの項目のメタデータが明示している部分です。回路は$n$個のHadamardと$\binom{n}{2}$個の制御位相ゲート、合計$O(n^2)$ゲートを使い、古典FFTが振幅ベクトル全体に対して行う$O(N\log N)=O(2^n\cdot n)$回の算術演算と比べて指数的にゲート数が少なくて済みますが、それは測定(サンプリング)しなければならない量子振幅に対してであり、追加コストなしで得られる古典的な出力ベクトルではありません。この項目のチェックはエクスポート経路を通したパーサ・コンパイル互換性の比較であり、数値的な回路正当性の証明ではありません。","exportStatus":"Lossless export classified · native Cirq and OpenQASM views","framework":"Cirq","introduction":"The QFT record emphasizes the metadata researchers need before reuse: wire count, phase-rotation structure, and what the export check actually covers.","introductionJa":"QFTでは、再利用前に量子ビット数、位相回転の構造、書き出し時に確認した範囲を重視します。","literature":[{"authors":"D. Coppersmith","relevance":"Analyzes an approximate QFT construction and the gate-count/precision trade-off this record describes.","relevanceJa":"近似QFT構成と、この項目が説明するゲート数・精度のトレードオフを分析します。","title":"An approximate Fourier transform useful in quantum factoring","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/0201067","year":"2002"},{"authors":"Michael A. Nielsen and Isaac L. Chuang","relevance":"Standard graduate textbook covering the single- and two-qubit gate definitions, matrix identities, and circuit primitives this record states.","relevanceJa":"この項目が示す1・2量子ビットゲートの定義、行列恒等式、回路プリミティブを扱う標準的な大学院教科書です。","title":"Quantum Computation and Quantum Information: 10th Anniversary Edition","url":"https://doi.org/10.1017/cbo9780511976667","year":"2010"}],"metadata":[{"label":"Gate family","value":"H + controlled phase"},{"label":"Bit order","value":"Swap layer explicit"},{"label":"Export","value":"QASM parse checked"}],"provenance":"Curated reference","relatedSlugs":["qaoa-maxcut-ring","hadamard-gate"],"resources":[{"label":"Qubits","value":"4"},{"label":"Depth","value":"18 gates"},{"label":"Rotation layers","value":"4"}],"slug":"qft-resource-screen","source":{"kind":"curated_reference","license":"CC BY 4.0-compatible reference metadata","reviewedBy":"LeonaQ curation pass","title":"An approximate Fourier transform useful in quantum factoring","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/0201067"},"sourceCoverage":{"hardware":"unknown","simulation":"unknown","theory":"unknown"},"status":"verified","tags":["resource estimate","cirq","qft","phase"],"title":"QFT resource screen","titleJa":"QFTリソース評価","topics":["algorithm-reference","phase-estimation"],"updatedAt":"2026-07-07","verification":"QASM parse · compilation compatibility passed","verificationDetails":{"method":"Circuit parser and gate-count comparison across the reference export path.","result":"Pass · phase rotation structure and qubit count are preserved."},"verificationMethods":["invariant_checks","research_paper"],"visualization":{"operations":[{"label":"H","qubits":[0],"tone":"accent"},{"label":"CP","qubits":[0,1],"tone":"ok"},{"label":"CP","qubits":[0,2],"tone":"ok"},{"label":"CP","qubits":[0,3],"tone":"ok"},{"label":"SWAP?","qubits":[0,3],"tone":"neutral"}],"outcomes":[{"label":"Phase-resolved basis","probability":0.75},{"label":"Other","probability":0.25}],"wires":["q[0]","q[1]","q[2]","q[3]"]}}

