FINAL_CIRCUIT = kernel","filename":"quantum_kernel.py","framework":"PennyLane","language":"python","note":"This returns a toy overlap estimate; training and held-out evaluation are intentionally separate from the circuit record.","status":"native"}],"description":"A quantum feature-map record paired with a classical SVM so model quality and data costs stay visible.","descriptionJa":"モデルの性能とデータ準備コストを比較するため、量子特徴写像と古典SVMを組み合わせた例です。","explanation":"The circuit prepares |φ(x)⟩ and uses overlap or a related measurement to estimate K(x, y). The classical SVM still performs the optimization; the quantum part changes the feature map.","explanationJa":"回路で|φ(x)⟩を準備し、重なりなどを測定してK(x,y)を推定します。最適化は古典SVMが行い、量子部分は特徴写像を変えます。","explanationMd":"A quantum kernel maps a classical input $x$ to a quantum state $|\phi(x)\rangle=U(x)|0\rangle$ via a feature-map circuit $U(x)$, and defines a kernel via the state overlap $K(x,y)=|\langle\phi(x)|\phi(y)\rangle|^2$. The circuit estimates $K(x,y)$ by applying $U(x)$ then $U(y)^\dagger$ and measuring the probability of returning to $|0\rangle^{\otimes n}$: $\Pr[0^n] = |\langle 0|U(y)^\dagger U(x)|0\rangle|^2 = K(x,y)$, so each entry of the kernel matrix costs repeated circuit shots rather than a closed-form evaluation. The resulting Gram matrix $K$ is handed to a standard classical SVM, which still performs the convex optimization over Lagrange multipliers — the quantum circuit only changes the feature map, not the learning algorithm. This record checks that $K$ is symmetric and numerically positive-semidefinite (within tolerance) on a small dataset; as its own caveat states, whether a given feature map's kernel actually separates a dataset better than a tuned classical kernel is a separate, data-dependent question this toy check does not answer.","explanationMdJa":"量子カーネルは、特徴写像回路$U(x)$によって古典入力$x$を量子状態$|\phi(x)\rangle=U(x)|0\rangle$に写し、状態の重なり $K(x,y)=|\langle\phi(x)|\phi(y)\rangle|^2$ でカーネルを定義します。回路は$U(x)$の後に$U(y)^\dagger$を適用し、$|0\rangle^{\otimes n}$に戻る確率を測定して$K(x,y)$を推定します: $\Pr[0^n] = |\langle 0|U(y)^\dagger U(x)|0\rangle|^2 = K(x,y)$。つまりカーネル行列の各要素は閉形式の計算ではなく反復ショットのコストがかかります。得られたグラム行列$K$は通常の古典SVMに渡され、ラグランジュ乗数についての凸最適化は古典SVM側が行います。量子回路が変えるのは特徴写像のみで、学習アルゴリズムではありません。この項目は小規模データセットで$K$が対称かつ(許容誤差内で)半正定値であることを確認しますが、その注記の通り、ある特徴写像のカーネルが調整済みの古典カーネルより実際にデータをよく分離するかは、この小規模な確認では答えられないデータ依存の別の問題です。","exportStatus":"Native PennyLane reference · Qiskit/Cirq conversions are circuit-level requests","framework":"PennyLane","industryUseCases":["High-energy physics classification","Small-data materials or sensor classification","Feature-map and kernel research"],"industryUseCasesJa":["高エネルギー物理の分類","小規模データの材料・センサー分類","特徴写像・カーネル研究"],"introduction":"Quantum kernels use a circuit to map inputs into a feature space and estimate similarities, then hand the kernel matrix to a classical learner. The meaningful benchmark is end-to-end predictive performance and cost.","introductionJa":"量子カーネルは回路で入力を特徴空間に写像し類似度を推定した後、カーネル行列を古典学習器に渡します。重要な比較は予測性能と総コストです。","literature":[{"authors":"Carsten Blank, Daniel K. Park, June-Koo Kevin Rhee, Francesco Petruccione","relevance":"Connects quantum-state fidelity kernels to a classifier and discusses a hardware demonstration.","relevanceJa":"量子状態忠実度カーネルと分類器を結びつけ、ハードウェア実証も議論します。","title":"Quantum classifier with tailored quantum kernel","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1909.02611","year":"2019"},{"authors":"Sau Lan Wu, Shaojun Sun, Wen Guan, Chen Zhou, Jay Chan, Chi Lung Cheng, Tuan Pham, Yan Qian, Alex Zeng Wang, Rui Zhang, Miron Livny, Jennifer Glick, Panagiotis Kl. Barkoutsos, Stefan Woerner, Ivano Tavernelli, Federico Carminati, Alberto Di Meglio, Andy C. Y. Li, Joseph Lykken, Panagiotis Spentzouris, Samuel Yen-Chi Chen, Shinjae Yoo, Tzu-Chieh Wei","relevance":"A domain application that reports quantum-kernel performance alongside classical counterparts.","relevanceJa":"量子カーネルの性能を古典手法と並べて報告するドメイン応用です。","title":"Application of Quantum Machine Learning using the Quantum Kernel Algorithm on High Energy 