s q;","filename":"s-phase.qasm","framework":"OpenQASM 3.0","language":"openqasm","status":"native"}],"description":"A quarter-turn phase gate that exposes the difference between global and relative phase.","descriptionJa":"グローバル位相と相対位相の違いを示す、4分の1回転の位相ゲートです。","explanation":"S|0⟩ = |0⟩ and S|1⟩ = i|1⟩. Because S² = Z, its phase convention can be checked without a large circuit.","explanationJa":"S|0⟩ = |0⟩、S|1⟩ = i|1⟩です。S² = Zなので、大きな回路なしに位相規約を確認できます。","explanationMd":"The $S$ gate (phase gate) is $S=\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\0&i\end{pmatrix}$, applying a $\pi/2$ phase to $|1\rangle$: $S|0\rangle=|0\rangle$, $S|1\rangle=i|1\rangle$. Squaring the matrix gives $S^2=\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\0&-1\end{pmatrix}=Z$, and applying it four times returns the identity, $S^4=I$ — exactly the power relations this record verifies by direct computation. $S$ is unitary but not Hermitian ($S^\dagger=S^{-1}=S^3\neq S$), and it is a Clifford gate: conjugating Pauli $X$ by $S$ gives $SXS^\dagger=Y$ up to sign convention, so $S$ maps the $X$/$Z$ stabilizer picture onto $Y$. Because $S=\sqrt Z$, it is the natural bridge between the Pauli group and finer phase rotations; composed with Hadamard it builds a $Y$-basis change of basis and, together with $T=\sqrt S$, generates approximately universal single-qubit rotations.","explanationMdJa":"$S$ゲート(位相ゲート)は $S=\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\0&i\end{pmatrix}$ で、$|1\rangle$に$\pi/2$の位相を与えます: $S|0\rangle=|0\rangle$、$S|1\rangle=i|1\rangle$。行列を二乗すると $S^2=\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\0&-1\end{pmatrix}=Z$ となり、4回適用すると恒等演算 $S^4=I$ に戻ります。これはこの項目が直接計算で確認するべき乗関係そのものです。$S$はユニタリですがエルミートではなく($S^\dagger=S^{-1}=S^3\neq S$)、クリフォードゲートの一つです。$S$で$X$を共役すると符号規約により $SXS^\dagger=Y$ となり、$X$/$Z$のスタビライザー描像を$Y$に写します。$S=\sqrt Z$であるため、パウリ群とより細かい位相回転をつなぐ自然な橋渡しであり、アダマールと組み合わせて$Y$基底への変換を作り、$T=\sqrt S$とともに近似的に万能な1量子ビット回転を生成します。","exportStatus":"Native OpenQASM 3 · direct framework snippets available","framework":"OpenQASM 3.0","introduction":"The S gate is a compact bridge from Pauli operators to controlled phase and Fourier-style circuits.","introductionJa":"Sゲートは、パウリ演算子から制御位相やフーリエ型回路へつなぐ小さな橋渡しです。","literature":[{"authors":"Michael A. Nielsen and Isaac L. Chuang","relevance":"Standard graduate textbook covering the single- and two-qubit gate definitions, matrix identities, and circuit primitives this record states.","relevanceJa":"この項目が示す1・2量子ビットゲートの定義、行列恒等式、回路プリミティブを扱う標準的な大学院教科書です。","title":"Quantum Computation and Quantum Information: 10th Anniversary Edition","url":"https://doi.org/10.1017/cbo9780511976667","year":"2010"}],"metadata":[{"label":"Matrix","value":"[[1, 0], [0, i]]"},{"label":"Power","value":"S² = Z"},{"label":"Family","value":"Clifford"}],"provenance":"Curated reference","relatedSlugs":["pauli-z-gate","t-phase-gate"],"resources":[{"label":"Qubits","value":"1"},{"label":"Depth","value":"1 gate"},{"label":"Phase","value":"π/2"}],"slug":"s-phase-gate","source":{"kind":"curated_reference","license":"CC BY 4.0-compatible reference metadata","reviewedBy":"Leona Quantum curation pass","title":"OpenQASM 3 standard gate set","url":"https://openqasm.com/language/gates.html"},"sourceCoverage":{"hardware":"unknown","simulation":"unknown","theory":"unknown"},"status":"verified","tags":["phase","clifford","single qubit"],"title":"S phase gate","titleJa":"S位相ゲート","topics":["gate-primitive","stabilizer"],"updatedAt":"2026-07-15","verification":"Power relation check · S² = Z and S⁴ = I","verificationDetails":{"method":"Evaluate the standard phase matrix and its repeated powers.","result":"Pass · S applies a π/2 phase to |1⟩ and composes to Z after two applications."},"verificationMethods":["unitary_equivalence","research_paper"],"visualization":{"operations":[{"label":"S","qubits":[0],"tone":"accent"}],"outcomes":[{"label":"Phase-resolved","probability":1}],"wires":["q[0]"]}}

{"algorithmFamily":"Quantum error correction","category":"operators","categoryLabel":"Operators","categoryLabelJa":"演算子","classicalComparison":{"baseline":"Classical parity-check codes and decoders provide an intuition for syndrome processing, but they do not preserve an unknown quantum phase.","baselineJa":"古典パリティ検査符号とデコーダはシンドローム処理の直感を与えますが、未知の量子位相は保存しません。","practicalRead":"Benchmark physical-versus-logical error rates, qubit and gate overhead, measurement rounds, decoder latency, and noise bias.","practicalReadJa":"物理・論理誤り率、量子ビットとゲートのオーバーヘッド、測定ラウンド、デコーダ遅延、ノイズ偏りを比較します。","quantumClaim":"A local quantum code can suppress logical errors below physical errors when the full architecture operates below its threshold.","quantumClaimJa":"全アーキテクチャが閾値以下で動作すれば、局所量子符号で論理誤りを物理誤りより抑えられる可能性があります。"},"codeVariants":[{"code":"OPENQASM 3.0;
