t q;","filename":"t-phase.qasm","framework":"OpenQASM 3.0","language":"openqasm","status":"native"}],"description":"A non-Clifford phase gate that marks the boundary between a compact Clifford set and universal synthesis.","descriptionJa":"クリフォード集合と普遍ゲート合成における位置づけを示す、非クリフォード位相ゲートです。","explanation":"T|0⟩ = |0⟩ and T|1⟩ = e^(iπ/4)|1⟩. Two T gates make S, and eight make the identity.","explanationJa":"T|0⟩ = |0⟩、T|1⟩ = e^(iπ/4)|1⟩です。Tを2回でS、8回で恒等になります。","explanationMd":"The $T$ gate is $T=\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\0&e^{i\pi/4}\end{pmatrix}$, applying a $\pi/4$ phase: $T|0\rangle=|0\rangle$, $T|1\rangle=e^{i\pi/4}|1\rangle$. Since $\left(e^{i\pi/4}\right)^2=e^{i\pi/2}=i$, direct matrix multiplication gives $T^2=S$ and $T^8=I$, exactly the power relations this record checks. Unlike $H$, $S$, $X$, $Y$, $Z$, $T$ is **not** a Clifford gate: conjugating $X$ by $T$ does not map it to another Pauli operator, which is precisely why $\{H, T\}$ is universal for quantum computation while Clifford-only circuits are efficiently classically simulable (Gottesman–Knill). This makes $T$ the standard "expensive" non-Clifford resource in fault-tolerant compilation: magic-state distillation exists specifically to produce high-fidelity $T$ gates from many noisy ones, since — as this record's own caveat notes — the ideal unitary identity above says nothing about a given device's hardware fidelity or noise.","explanationMdJa":"$T$ゲートは $T=\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\0&e^{i\pi/4}\end{pmatrix}$ で、$\pi/4$の位相を与えます: $T|0\rangle=|0\rangle$、$T|1\rangle=e^{i\pi/4}|1\rangle$。$\left(e^{i\pi/4}\right)^2=e^{i\pi/2}=i$ なので、直接計算で $T^2=S$、$T^8=I$ が得られ、これがこの項目が確認するべき乗関係です。$H$、$S$、$X$、$Y$、$Z$と異なり、$T$はクリフォードゲートではありません。$T$で$X$を共役しても別のパウリ演算子にはならず、これが$\{H,T\}$が量子計算にとって万能である一方、クリフォードのみの回路は効率的に古典シミュレートできる(Gottesman–Knill)理由です。このためフォールトトレラント実装では$T$が高コストな非クリフォード資源として扱われ、多数のノイズ入り$T$から高忠実度な$T$を作るマジック状態蒸留が使われます。この項目自身の注記の通り、上記の理想ユニタリ恒等式は特定デバイスのハードウェア忠実度やノイズについては何も主張しません。","exportStatus":"Native OpenQASM 3 · direct framework snippets available","framework":"OpenQASM 3.0","introduction":"T is useful in resource discussions because its ideal matrix is simple while fault-tolerant cost can dominate.","introductionJa":"Tは理想行列が単純でもフォールトトレラントなコストが支配的になり得るため、リソース議論に有用です。","literature":[{"authors":"Michael A. Nielsen and Isaac L. Chuang","relevance":"Standard graduate textbook covering the single- and two-qubit gate definitions, matrix identities, and circuit primitives this record states.","relevanceJa":"この項目が示す1・2量子ビットゲートの定義、行列恒等式、回路プリミティブを扱う標準的な大学院教科書です。","title":"Quantum Computation and Quantum Information: 10th Anniversary Edition","url":"https://doi.org/10.1017/cbo9780511976667","year":"2010"}],"metadata":[{"label":"Matrix","value":"[[1, 0], [0, e^(iπ/4)]]"},{"label":"Power","value":"T² = S"},{"label":"Family","value":"Non-Clifford"}],"provenance":"Curated reference","relatedSlugs":["s-phase-gate","qft-resource-screen"],"resources":[{"label":"Qubits","value":"1"},{"label":"Depth","value":"1 gate"},{"label":"Phase","value":"π/4"}],"slug":"t-phase-gate","source":{"kind":"curated_reference","license":"CC BY 4.0-compatible reference metadata","reviewedBy":"Leona Quantum curation pass","title":"OpenQASM 3 standard gate set","url":"https://openqasm.com/language/gates.html"},"sourceCoverage":{"hardware":"unknown","simulation":"unknown","theory":"unknown"},"status":"verified_caveats","tags":["phase","non-clifford","fault tolerant"],"title":"T phase gate","titleJa":"T位相ゲート","topics":["gate-primitive","error-correction"],"updatedAt":"2026-07-15","verification":"Power relation check · T² = S and T⁸ = I","verificationDetails":{"caveat":"This record verifies the ideal unitary relation; hardware fidelity and noise are not claimed.","method":"Evaluate the standard π/4 phase matrix and repeated powers.","result":"Pass · T applies a π/4 phase to |1⟩."},"verificationMethods":["unitary_equivalence","research_paper"],"visualization":{"operations":[{"label":"T","qubits":[0],"tone":"warn"}],"outcomes":[{"label":"Phase-resolved","probability":1}],"wires":["q[0]"]}}

{"algorithmFamily":"Variational quantum algorithm","category":"algorithms","categoryLabel":"Algorithms","categoryLabelJa":"アルゴリズム","classicalComparison":{"baseline":"Exact diagonalization for small Hamiltonians; coupled-cluster, DMRG, tensor networks, or other electronic-structure methods at scale.","baselineJa":"小さなハミルトニアンでは厳密対角化、大きな系ではCC、DMRG、テンソルネットワーク等を比較します。","practicalRead":"Compare energy error, total shots, circuit depth, optimizer calls, basis/mapping choices, and classical wall-clock time.","practicalReadJa":"エネルギー誤差、総ショット数、回路深さ、最適化呼び出し数、基底・写像、古典実時間を比較します。","quantumClaim":"VQE can estimate a variational energy using shallow circuits plus a classical optimizer, not an automatic advantage over mature chemistry software.","quantumClaimJa":"VQEは浅い回路と古典最適化器で変分エネルギーを推定しますが、成熟した化学ソフトウェアに対する自動的な優位性ではありません。"},"codeVariants":[{"code":"import pennylane as qml
from pennylane import numpy as np

dev = qml.device("default.qubit", wires=2)
H = qml.Hamiltonian([0.5, 0.5], [qml.PauliZ(0), qml.PauliZ(1)])

@qml.qnode(dev)
def energy(theta):
    qml.RY(theta[0], wires=0)
    qml.CNOT(wires=[0, 1])
