FINAL_CIRCUIT = energy","filename":"vqe_energy.py","framework":"PennyLane","language":"python","note":"The fixture demonstrates the hybrid loop shape; it is not a molecular chemistry benchmark.","status":"native"}],"description":"A hybrid chemistry workflow that compares a quantum expectation loop with classical eigensolvers.","descriptionJa":"量子期待値ループと古典固有値ソルバーを比較する、ハイブリッドな化学ワークフローです。","explanation":"The variational principle guarantees an energy upper bound for a normalized trial state. Reaching a useful answer still requires a good encoding, ansatz, optimizer, and measurement budget.","explanationJa":"変分原理により、正規化された試行状態のエネルギーは上限になります。実用的な答えには符号化、ansatz、最適化器、測定予算が必要です。","explanationMd":"VQE estimates a ground-state energy using the variational principle: for any normalized trial state $|\psi(\theta)\rangle=U(\theta)|0\rangle$ and Hamiltonian $H$, the Rayleigh quotient obeys $\langle\psi(\theta)|H|\psi(\theta)\rangle \ge E_0$, the true ground energy, with equality only when $|\psi(\theta)\rangle$ is an exact ground eigenstate. The circuit prepares $|\psi(\theta)\rangle$ with a parameterized ansatz $U(\theta)$, measures each Pauli term of $H=\sum_k c_k P_k$ to build $\langle H\rangle(\theta)$, and hands that scalar to a classical optimizer that updates $\theta$ to push the energy down — a hybrid quantum/classical loop repeated to convergence. This record checks that expectation-value loop for a small Pauli Hamiltonian against exact diagonalization, matching its own caveat: the variational *bound* is guaranteed by the math above, but reaching a chemically useful energy still depends on ansatz expressivity, optimizer convergence, and shot noise this toy fixture does not certify.","explanationMdJa":"VQEは変分原理を使って基底状態エネルギーを推定します。正規化された試行状態$|\psi(\theta)\rangle=U(\theta)|0\rangle$とハミルトニアン$H$に対し、Rayleigh商は $\langle\psi(\theta)|H|\psi(\theta)\rangle \ge E_0$(真の基底エネルギー)を満たし、等号は$|\psi(\theta)\rangle$が厳密な基底固有状態のときだけ成立します。回路はパラメータ付きansatz $U(\theta)$で$|\psi(\theta)\rangle$を準備し、$H=\sum_k c_k P_k$の各パウリ項を測定して$\langle H\rangle(\theta)$を構成し、そのスカラーを古典最適化器に渡してエネルギーを下げる方向に$\theta$を更新します。これを収束まで繰り返すハイブリッド量子・古典ループです。この項目は、この期待値ループを小さなパウリハミルトニアンについて厳密対角化と比較しており、このエントリ自身の注記と一致します。上記の数学が保証するのは変分「上限」であり、化学的に有用なエネルギーに到達できるかはansatzの表現力、最適化の収束、ショットノイズに依存し、このトイの検証はそれらを保証しません。","exportStatus":"Native PennyLane · Qiskit conversion is straightforward for Pauli terms","framework":"PennyLane","industryUseCases":["Molecular ground states and reaction energies","Materials and catalyst screening","Hybrid quantum chemistry prototyping"],"industryUseCasesJa":["分子基底状態と反応エネルギー","材料・触媒スクリーニング","ハイブリッド量子化学プロトタイピング"],"introduction":"VQE combines a parameterized state, repeated measurements of a Hamiltonian, and a classical optimizer. It remains an important NISQ-era chemistry pattern because it trades deep coherent evolution for repeated shallow experiments.","introductionJa":"VQEはパラメータ付き状態、ハミルトニアンの反復測定、古典最適化器を組み合わせます。深いコヒーレント発展を浅い実験の反復に置き換えるため、NISQ時代の化学パターンとして重要です。","literature":[{"authors":"Alberto Peruzzo, Jarrod McClean, Peter Shadbolt, Man-Hong Yung, Xiao-Qi Zhou, Peter J. Love, Alán Aspuru-Guzik, Jeremy L. O'Brien","relevance":"Original VQE proposal and photonic demonstration for a small chemistry problem.","relevanceJa":"小さな化学問題でのVQE提案とフォトニック実証を示す原論文です。","title":"A variational eigenvalue solver on a quantum processor","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1304.3061","year":"2013"},{"authors":"R. J. P. T. de Keijzer, V. E. Colussi, B. Škorić, S. J. J. M. F. Kokkelmans","relevance":"Surveys optimizer, ansatz, and measurement choices that affect chemistry-oriented VQE runs.","relevanceJa":"化学向けVQEで効く最適化器、ansatz、測定設計を比較します。","title":"Optimization of the Variational Quantum Eigensolver for Quantum Chemistry Applications","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2102.01781","year":"2021"}],"metadata":[{"label":"Hamiltonian","value":"Pauli sum"},{"label":"Optimizer","value":"Classical"},{"label":"Reference","value":"Exact diagonalization"},{"label":"Main risk","value":"Convergence + shots"}]